# Copy to .env and adjust. Every value here is optional -- the app runs with
# sensible defaults when .env is absent.

# Per-request timeout, in seconds. Reasoning-capable models on hard questions
# can think for well over the previous 120s limit; when the read times out the
# run fails with no answer.
#
# LLM_COUNCIL_REQUEST_TIMEOUT applies to every provider. A provider-specific
# {PROVIDER}_REQUEST_TIMEOUT overrides it -- ANTHROPIC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT,
# OPENAI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT, OPENCODE_ZEN_REQUEST_TIMEOUT, and so on.
#
# The 180s default is deliberately not unbounded: a council round queries
# several models in parallel, and a stalled provider holds its slot for the
# whole timeout. Raise it for the providers that need it rather than globally.
# LLM_COUNCIL_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=180
# ANTHROPIC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=600
